# Ant Design Quick Start Tutorial

## Table of Contents
1. [Introduction](#introduction)
2. [Installation](#installation)
3. [Basic Setup](#basic-setup)
4. [First Component](#first-component)
5. [Common Components](#common-components)
6. [Layout System](#layout-system)
7. [Form Handling](#form-handling)
8. [Best Practices](#best-practices)
9. [Resources](#resources)

## Introduction

Ant Design (antd) is a popular React UI library that provides high-quality components and demos for building rich, interactive user interfaces. It follows the Ant Design specification and is widely used in enterprise-level applications.

### Key Features
- 🎨 Rich set of high-quality components
- 📱 Responsive design out of the box
- 🌐 Internationalization support
- 🎯 TypeScript support
- 📊 Customizable themes
- 🔧 Accessible and WAI-ARIA compliant

## Installation

### Using npm
```bash
npm install antd
```

### Using yarn
```bash
yarn add antd
```

### Using pnpm
```bash
pnpm add antd
```

## Basic Setup

### 1. Import Ant Design CSS
In your main entry file (e.g., `src/index.js` or `src/main.js`):

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom/client';
import 'antd/dist/reset.css'; // Import Ant Design styles
import App from './App';

const root = ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root'));
root.render(<App />);
```

### 2. Configure Ant Design (Optional)
For advanced configuration, you can use the `ConfigProvider`:

```javascript
import { ConfigProvider } from 'antd';
import zhCN from 'antd/locale/zh_CN';

function App() {
  return (
    <ConfigProvider locale={zhCN}>
      {/* Your app components */}
    </ConfigProvider>
  );
}
```

## First Component

Let's create a simple button example:

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import { Button } from 'antd';

function MyFirstComponent() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>My First Ant Design Component</h2>
      <Button type="primary">Click Me!</Button>
      <Button>Default</Button>
      <Button type="dashed">Dashed</Button>
      <Button type="text">Text</Button>
      <Button type="link">Link</Button>
    </div>
  );
}

export default MyFirstComponent;
```

### Button Types
- `primary`: Primary button for main actions
- `default`: Default button
- `dashed`: Dashed button
- `text`: Text button
- `link`: Link button

### Button States
```jsx
<Button type="primary" loading>Loading...</Button>
<Button type="primary" disabled>Disabled</Button>
<Button danger>Danger</Button>
```

## Common Components

### 1. Typography
```jsx
import { Typography } from 'antd';

const { Title, Paragraph, Text } = Typography;

function TypographyExample() {
  return (
    <Typography>
      <Title level={1}>Heading 1</Title>
      <Title level={2}>Heading 2</Title>
      <Title level={3}>Heading 3</Title>
      <Paragraph>
        This is a paragraph with <Text type="danger">danger text</Text> and 
        <Text type="success">success text</Text>.
      </Paragraph>
    </Typography>
  );
}
```

### 2. Input Components
```jsx
import { Input, Select, DatePicker } from 'antd';

const { Option } = Select;

function InputExample() {
  return (
    <div style={{ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: '16px' }}>
      <Input placeholder="Basic input" />
      <Input.Password placeholder="Password input" />
      <Input.Search placeholder="Search input" />

      <Select defaultValue="option1" style={{ width: '100%' }}>
        <Option value="option1">Option 1</Option>
        <Option value="option2">Option 2</Option>
        <Option value="option3">Option 3</Option>
      </Select>

      <DatePicker style={{ width: '100%' }} />
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 3. Table
```jsx
import { Table } from 'antd';

const dataSource = [
  {
    key: '1',
    name: 'John Doe',
    age: 32,
    address: '123 Main St',
  },
  {
    key: '2',
    name: 'Jane Smith',
    age: 28,
    address: '456 Oak Ave',
  },
];

const columns = [
  {
    title: 'Name',
    dataIndex: 'name',
    key: 'name',
  },
  {
    title: 'Age',
    dataIndex: 'age',
    key: 'age',
  },
  {
    title: 'Address',
    dataIndex: 'address',
    key: 'address',
  },
];

function TableExample() {
  return <Table dataSource={dataSource} columns={columns} />;
}
```

### 4. Modal
```jsx
import { Modal, Button } from 'antd';
import { useState } from 'react';

function ModalExample() {
  const [isModalOpen, setIsModalOpen] = useState(false);

  const showModal = () => {
    setIsModalOpen(true);
  };

  const handleOk = () => {
    setIsModalOpen(false);
  };

  const handleCancel = () => {
    setIsModalOpen(false);
  };

  return (
    <>
      <Button type="primary" onClick={showModal}>
        Open Modal
      </Button>
      <Modal
        title="Basic Modal"
        open={isModalOpen}
        onOk={handleOk}
        onCancel={handleCancel}
      >
        <p>Some contents...</p>
        <p>Some contents...</p>
        <p>Some contents...</p>
      </Modal>
    </>
  );
}
```

## Layout System

Ant Design provides a powerful layout system with `Layout`, `Row`, and `Col` components.

### Basic Layout
```jsx
import { Layout, Menu } from 'antd';

const { Header, Content, Footer } = Layout;

function LayoutExample() {
  return (
    <Layout>
      <Header style={{ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'center' }}>
        <div style={{ color: 'white', fontSize: '18px', marginRight: '20px' }}>
          Logo
        </div>
        <Menu theme="dark" mode="horizontal" style={{ flex: 1 }}>
          <Menu.Item key="1">Home</Menu.Item>
          <Menu.Item key="2">About</Menu.Item>
          <Menu.Item key="3">Contact</Menu.Item>
        </Menu>
      </Header>

      <Content style={{ padding: '0 50px', marginTop: '24px' }}>
        <div style={{ background: '#fff', padding: 24, minHeight: 280 }}>
          Content
        </div>
      </Content>

      <Footer style={{ textAlign: 'center' }}>
        Ant Design ©2023 Created by Your Name
      </Footer>
    </Layout>
  );
}
```

### Grid System
```jsx
import { Row, Col, Card } from 'antd';

function GridExample() {
  return (
    <Row gutter={[16, 16]}>
      <Col span={8}>
        <Card title="Card title" bordered={false}>
          Card content
        </Card>
      </Col>
      <Col span={8}>
        <Card title="Card title" bordered={false}>
          Card content
        </Card>
      </Col>
      <Col span={8}>
        <Card title="Card title" bordered={false}>
          Card content
        </Card>
      </Col>

      <Col span={12}>
        <Card title="Wide card" bordered={false}>
          This card takes 12 columns
        </Card>
      </Col>
      <Col span={12}>
        <Card title="Wide card" bordered={false}>
          This card takes 12 columns
        </Card>
      </Col>
    </Row>
  );
}
```

## Form Handling

Ant Design provides excellent form handling with the `Form` component.

### Basic Form
```jsx
import { Form, Input, Button, Select, DatePicker } from 'antd';

const { Option } = Select;

function MyForm() {
  const [form] = Form.useForm();

  const onFinish = (values) => {
    console.log('Form values:', values);
  };

  const onFinishFailed = (errorInfo) => {
    console.log('Failed:', errorInfo);
  };

  return (
    <Form
      form={form}
      layout="vertical"
      onFinish={onFinish}
      onFinishFailed={onFinishFailed}
      autoComplete="off"
    >
      <Form.Item
        label="Username"
        name="username"
        rules={[{ required: true, message: 'Please input your username!' }]}
      >
        <Input />
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item
        label="Email"
        name="email"
        rules={[
          { required: true, message: 'Please input your email!' },
          { type: 'email', message: 'Please enter a valid email!' }
        ]}
      >
        <Input />
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item
        label="Gender"
        name="gender"
        rules={[{ required: true, message: 'Please select gender!' }]}
      >
        <Select placeholder="Select your gender">
          <Option value="male">Male</Option>
          <Option value="female">Female</Option>
          <Option value="other">Other</Option>
        </Select>
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item
        label="Birth Date"
        name="birthDate"
        rules={[{ required: true, message: 'Please select your birth date!' }]}
      >
        <DatePicker style={{ width: '100%' }} />
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item>
        <Button type="primary" htmlType="submit">
          Submit
        </Button>
      </Form.Item>
    </Form>
  );
}
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Component Organization
```jsx
// Good: Organize components by feature
// components/User/
// ├── UserList.js
// ├── UserForm.js
// └── UserProfile.js

// Good: Use consistent naming conventions
import { Button, Input, Form } from 'antd';
import { UserOutlined, LockOutlined } from '@ant-design/icons';
```

### 2. Performance Optimization
```jsx
import React, { memo } from 'react';
import { Table } from 'antd';

// Use memo for components that don't need to re-render often
const OptimizedTable = memo(({ data, columns }) => {
  return <Table dataSource={data} columns={columns} rowKey="id" />;
});

// Use pagination for large datasets
const PaginatedTable = () => {
  return (
    <Table
      dataSource={largeDataSet}
      columns={columns}
      pagination={{ pageSize: 10 }}
      scroll={{ y: 400 }}
    />
  );
};
```

### 3. Accessibility
```jsx
import { Button, Input } from 'antd';

// Always provide proper labels and ARIA attributes
function AccessibleForm() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Input
        placeholder="Enter your name"
        aria-label="Full name"
        aria-describedby="name-help"
      />
      <span id="name-help" style={{ fontSize: '12px', color: '#666' }}>
        Please enter your full name
      </span>

      <Button 
        type="primary"
        aria-label="Submit form"
      >
        Submit
      </Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 4. Error Handling
```jsx
import { message, notification } from 'antd';

function ErrorHandler() {
  const handleAsyncOperation = async () => {
    try {
      // Your async operation
      await someAsyncFunction();
      message.success('Operation completed successfully!');
    } catch (error) {
      message.error('Operation failed. Please try again.');
      notification.error({
        message: 'Error',
        description: error.message,
        duration: 4,
      });
    }
  };

  return (
    <Button onClick={handleAsyncOperation}>
      Start Operation
    </Button>
  );
}
```

